8. What are the wait() and sleep() methods?

wait()
    non-static method
     current thread to wait and go to sleep until some other threads call the notify () or notifyAll()
     It simply releases the lock and is mostly used for inter-thread communication.
      It is defined in the object class,
      and should only be called from a synchronized context.

      synchronized(monitor)
      {
      monitor.wait();       Here Lock Is Released by Current Thread
      }


sleep()

     static method
      pauses or stops the execution of the current thread for some specified period.
       It doesn’t release the lock
       It is defined in thread class,
        and no need to call from a synchronized context

